No score assigned.

**Reused evidence**
No prior evidence item cleanly reuses as substantive 7B evidence. Prior identity/office context was used only for attribution, not as integrity evidence.

**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"อ่านฉบับเต็ม คกก.วินิจฉัยการเปิดเผยข้อมูลข่าวสารคณะ3 สั่งป.ป.ช.เปิดเซฟ บิ๊กตู่ -วิษณุ","publisher":"Matichon","publication_date":"2021-08-20","url":"https://www.matichon.co.th/local/news_2896395","claim":"An information-commission ruling ordered the NACC to open the asset declarations of Prayut Chan-o-cha and Wissanu Krea-ngam for public inspection, after the NACC refused to disclose the 2019 filings that the two had submitted as evidence.","locator":"lines 131-142 and 147-152","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"The article reproduces the official ruling details and the NACC's refusal rationale with specific case numbers and dates.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The ruling and underlying disclosure dispute were live in the Prayut target-period and still relevant in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Prayut as the office-holder whose own asset filing was being withheld from public inspection; the ruling also concerns Wissanu.","contrary_evidence":["NACC argued the evidence filing was private and not legally disclosable.","The article reports the official dispute rather than a finding of substantive corruption."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"แค่ส่งคำตอบทางการ “ให้ดูไม่ได้” ยังใช้เวลา 8 เดือนเต็ม ป.ป.ช.ไม่เปิดบัญชีประยุทธ์-วิษณุ","publisher":"The MATTER","publication_date":"2022-04-28","url":"https://thematter.co/brief/173609/173609","claim":"Eight months after the formal request, the NACC still had not answered whether the public could inspect Prayut Chan-o-cha's and Wissanu Krea-ngam's 2019 asset accounts.","locator":"opening paragraph / first summary paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous coverage of an ongoing official disclosure dispute, though it remains a journalistic summary rather than a primary document.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly contemporaneous with 2022 and squarely within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Prayut because the nondisclosed accounts were his second-term asset filings; the obstruction is institutional rather than a confession of wrongdoing.","contrary_evidence":["NACC said the law did not authorize disclosure of filings submitted 'as evidence'.","This shows opacity, not a proven hidden asset or illicit gain."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Explainer-How a Thai court suspended Prime Minister Prayuth","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-08-25","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/08/25/thailand-politics-suspension","claim":"After the Constitutional Court suspended Prayuth pending term-limit review, government spokesman Anucha Burapachaisri said Prayuth respected the court's decision, had ceased active duty, and urged the public to respect the decision and avoid further division.","locator":"lines 642-665 and 657-659","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with direct attribution to the government spokesman and the court's official action.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut's conduct in office because he complied with and publicly acknowledged the court suspension.","contrary_evidence":["The suspension itself arose from a contested term-limit petition and opposition efforts to remove him.","Compliance does not answer broader honesty or self-dealing questions."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thai court clears way for PM Prayuth's return from suspension","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-10-01","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/10/01/thailand-politics","claim":"The court ruled Prayuth had not exceeded the eight-year limit; in a Facebook post he said his limited time should be used to push important projects, while the opposition said the verdict did not cleanse him and that he had broken his promise not to stay long.","locator":"period-of-reflection section and the opposition statement near the end of the article","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a formal court verdict plus contemporaneous quotations from Prayuth and the opposition.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Prayut because it captures his own public framing of continued rule and the opposition's counterclaim about his broken promise.","contrary_evidence":["The court ruled in his favor and did not find him disqualified.","The article mixes his statement with opposition criticism, so it is a mixed integrity signal rather than proof of deception."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thai opposition files no-confidence motion against 'flawed' PM","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-06-16","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/06/16/us-thailand-politics","claim":"Thailand's opposition filed a no-confidence motion accusing Prayuth of graft, economic mismanagement, undermining democracy and clinging to power, while the government spokesman said the administration was confident it ran the country honestly without corruption.","locator":"opening paragraphs / opposition and government quoted statements","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report captures both the accusation and the official rebuttal in the same 2022 parliamentary episode.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"The accusation is directed at Prayut personally, but it remains an opposition allegation rather than a finding.","contrary_evidence":["No judicial or audit finding of graft is reported in the article.","Government denial means this is disputed, not established."],"lenses":["7B.7","7B.8","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thai opposition seeks court ruling to halt move to change election system","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-07-08","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/07/08/us-thailand-politics","claim":"Opposition leaders said pro-administration lawmakers were trying to change the electoral system to favour smaller parties that had helped Prayuth build his 17-party coalition and argued that he wanted to remain in power by using the system as his tool.","locator":"lines 660-669","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters provides the legislative change and the opposition's account of its purpose with direct quotations.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but substantial: the move is attributed to pro-government lawmakers and the coalition structure serving Prayut's continued rule.","contrary_evidence":["Government spokesman said the changes reflected the parliamentary majority and had nothing to do with Prayuth or his administration.","This remains an allegation about motive, not a judicial finding."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Minnows to aid PPRP at poll","publisher":"Bangkok Post","publication_date":"2022-07-18","url":"https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/politics/2347903/minnows-to-aid-pprp-at-poll","claim":"Two small parties were expected to serve as offshoots to support the ruling Palang Pracharath Party, and the article says key figures in those parties were known close associates of Prayut Chan-o-cha and Prawit Wongsuwon.","locator":"article body near the opening summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Mainstream Thai newspaper reporting on coalition engineering and close-associate networks during the 2022 election cycle.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the network is linked to Prayut's political circle, but the article does not prove his direct order or private benefit.","contrary_evidence":["The article describes expectation and observer judgment, not a formal finding of nepotism or corruption.","Close association is not itself proof of personal enrichment."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"'No reshuffle,' says defiant PM","publisher":"Bangkok Post","publication_date":"2022-07-23","url":"https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/politics/2352066/no-reshuffle-says-defiant-pm","claim":"After the censure debate, Prayut denied a cabinet reshuffle, said he had not thought about it yet, and the article reports that he met Group of 16 MPs asking them to back the cabinet ministers targeted in the no-confidence motion.","locator":"lines 181-195","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct reporting of Prayuth's own statement and coalition-management activity during the 2022 censure cycle.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 fit.","ruler_attribution":"Direct but limited: this shows Prayut personally managing coalition support and appointments, though not personal self-enrichment.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not prove unethical conduct by itself.","Coalition bargaining can be ordinary politics absent additional evidence."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.9"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- Screened roughly 30 documents across Reuters/Euronews mirrors, Matichon, The MATTER, Bangkok Post, Thai Newsroom, Nation, iLaw, and NACC/OIC-related pages.
- Accepted the six 2022-relevant integrity items above plus one 2021 ruling summary because it directly governs the 2022 disclosure dispute around Prayut's second-term asset filings.
- Rejected or downgraded duplicate Reuters mirrors that repeated the same term-limit or coalition story without adding a new claim.
- Rejected 2023-2025 NACC notices and asset-disclosure pages as out of period unless they were only used as background.
- Rejected older watch-scandal coverage and general corruption-index material as background only, because they did not add a 2022 personal-nexus claim.
- Rejected broad Thailand corruption, repression, or governance reports when they lacked a direct link to Prayut's own truthfulness, asset disclosure, appointment choices, or obstruction of scrutiny.
- No document produced a direct 2022 finding of Prayut family enrichment or a judicial finding of personal fraud.

**Remaining gaps**
- The biggest gap is direct 2022 proof of personal enrichment, hidden assets, gifts, procurement benefit, or family profit.
- I found better evidence on disclosure opacity than on actual concealed wealth, so the dossier is stronger on obstruction of scrutiny than on proven self-dealing.
- More search would help on any 2022 NACC asset release for Prayut, cabinet-appointment documentation, and procurement or licensing decisions tied specifically to him.
- More Thai-language reporting could sharpen whether he personally instructed opacity or merely benefited from a legal loophole.
- The current record is enough to show a mixed but thin integrity pattern, not enough to establish central, ruler-specific kleptocracy.
